# watch-mailbox/_source/0 — receive one pulled message.
#
# The source poller fires ONE run of this stack per new message it read
# from the watched mailbox. The parsed message is at @source.msg (the
# same shape an LMTP delivery lands at @lmtp.msg); @source.key is a
# stable dedup id, "<uidvalidity>:<uid>".
#
# Delivery is AT-LEAST-ONCE: a crash between this run succeeding and the
# poller's move re-delivers the message next poll. So record it with a
# check-and-set keyed by @source.key and NO `expected` — a plain write
# that lands only when the key is absent. A redelivery finds the key
# already there (._rec.swapped == false) and changes nothing. The
# `received` namespace buckets these so GET /received can list them
# (kv/list returns the keys of a namespace; the key IS @source.key).
#
# We emit nothing to @source.res.action, so the source's declared
# on_processed applies — the message is MOVEd to "Processed" once this
# run reaches a successful terminal. (To send a handled and a rejected
# message to different folders, a rule here would
# `EMIT @source.res.action = "move:Rejected"`; valid actions are
# move:<folder>, seen, none.)
WHEN @source.key != ""
  EXEC "txco://kv/cas"
    WITH namespace = "received",
         key = @source.key,
         value = &object(
           "key", @source.key,
           "subject", @source.msg.subject,
           "from", @source.msg.from.0.addr,
           "fetched_at", @source.fetched_at),
         into = "._rec"
